ted separately.\n\n- ${{2}}$ and ${{∅}}$ each count as single elements of $Y.$\n\nSince $Y$ has $6$ elements, the cardinality is $|Y|=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-80447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24ce056e-1fe1-55d4-b88c-62629435003b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181589/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "646b3f76-235f-53e1-9aa6-63221e8e9ade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181589/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "9b28d0eb-e93f-5a14-b5cd-297ff9e38876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051865 :answer-field/correct "q-181589/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-181589/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-181589/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181589"] :question/problem "If $T={{},x,y,{v,x,{w}}},$ then $|T|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $T$ is the number of elements in $T.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $T:$\n\n$$\n{},\\,x,\\,y,\\,{v,x,{w}},\n$$\n\nNote that ${v,x,{w}}$ and ${}$ count as single elements of $T.$\n\nSince $T$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|T|=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80737/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3e346c35-aca2-5a79-a28e-1aa51f7911f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80737/selec