}}\n$$\n\nNote that $∅,$ ${∅},$ and ${{∅}}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80737/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24ce056e-1fe1-55d4-b88c-62629435003b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80737"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181563/field-1/df94e31932731dad0d3f3d6ebf3ae9c013e1315c1725c823caccda47f6038566" :answer/id #uuid "81e53f55-af8d-51fb-a296-b63e29304373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "172" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051856 :answer-field/correct "q-181563/field-1/df94e31932731dad0d3f3d6ebf3ae9c013e1315c1725c823caccda47f6038566" :answer-field/choices ["q-181563/field-1/df94e31932731dad0d3f3d6ebf3ae9c013e1315c1725c823caccda47f6038566"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181563"] :question/problem "If $A={-200,-193,-186,…,997},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-200,\\,-193,\\,-186,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =7 \\\\  & =-193-(-200) \\\\  & =-186-(-193) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-200+(n-1)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =-200+7n-7 \\\\  & =7n-207.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={7n-207:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7N-207 & =997 \\\\ 7N & =1\\,204 \\\\ N & =\\frac{1\\,204}{7} \\\\ N & =172\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={7n-207:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 172}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $172$ elements, we must have $|A|=172.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-181564/field-1/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "650eb2e2-6d72-5768-941a-777254debf85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181564/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "7d84f4ab-176f-5135-9878-24d2edd65ce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181564/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f651eb26-4e2c-5118-b8bb-0d82665314d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181564/field-1/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer-field/choices ["q-181564/field-1/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" "q-181564/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181564" :question/id #uuid "4dbe27ab-40a5-53ce-97e8-2ca064c299b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-181564" :question/problem "If $A={-8,-5,-2,…,184},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-8,\\,-5,\\,-2,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =-5-(-8) \\\\  & =-2-(-5) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-8+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={3n-11:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3N-11 & =184 \\\\ 3N & =195 \\\\ N & =\\frac{195}{3} \\\\ N & =65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={3n-11:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 65}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $65$ elements, we must have $|A|=65.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181564/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181565/field-1/b89a17384cd782bd6590754a469a452a13eb727e847613ba265e6de7afeda895" :answer/id #uuid "cb6e95c6-7061-5fed-a14f-bc6af96b9b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1371" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181565/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1333043c-4319-5cbb-9554-f2ba3278f0a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181565/field-1/b89a17384cd782bd6590754a469a452a13eb727e847613ba265e6de7afeda895" :answer-field/choices ["q-181565/field-1/b89a17384cd782bd6590754a469a452a13eb727e847613ba265e6de7afeda895"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181565" :question/id #uuid "4b782cd9-71cd-51a7-8679-e22d2b29be22" :question/math-academy-id "q-181565" :question/problem "If $A={-1\\,250,-1\\,235,-1\\,220,…,19\\,300},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-1\\,250,\\,-1\\,235,\\,-1\\,220,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=15:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =15 \\\\  & =-1\\,235-(-1\\,250) \\\\  & =-1\\,220-(-1\\,235) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-1\\,250\\,+(n-1)\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =-1\\,250+15n-15 \\\\  & =15n-1\\,265.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={15n-1\\,265:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15N-1\\,265 & =19\\,300 \\\\ 15N & =20\\,565 \\\\ N & =\\frac{20\\,565}{15} \\\\ N & =1\\,371\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={15n-1\\,265:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 1\\,371}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $1\\,371$ elements, we must have $|A|=1\\,371.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181565/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181565"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181559/field-1/b14754da480bd946dd2cc3567700940c490aee4fa777176509a9d997264e1d80" :answer/id #uuid "91361b35-1806-56a5-a47c-db4792c5aa9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "316" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181559/field-1/76da391199c7c0055883be9f3f4e9942c2c66c2d57814df96f93a604bb6b0dd0" :answer/id #uuid "7d1402c5-4acc-517b-957d-5e989e7f6bab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "315" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181559/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae666fef-4750-5c6e-be96-688bcbe5b75d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181559/field-1/b14754da480bd946dd2cc3567700940c490aee4fa777176509a9d997264e1d80" :answer-field/choices ["q-181559/field-1/b14754da480bd946dd2cc3567700940c490aee4fa777176509a9d997264e1d80" "q-181559/field-1/76da391199c7c0055883be9f3f4e9942c2c66c2d57814df96f93a604bb6b0dd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181559" :question/id #uuid "49131e72-c8a0-59f3-99af-aa1dff260098" :question/math-academy-id "q-181559" :question/problem "If $A={15,21,27,…,1\\,905},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n15,\\,21,\\,27,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =6 \\\\  & =21-15 \\\\  & =27-21 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =15+(n-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =15+6n-6 \\\\  & =6n+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={6n+9:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6N+9 & =1\\,905 \\\\ 6N & =1\\,896 \\\\ N & =\\frac{1\\,896}{6} \\\\ N & =316\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={6n+9:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 316}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $316$ elements, we must have $|A|=316.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181559/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181562/field-1/c69326908621995e0249ba36542f1b320610157ba12a69fa8d791492ca6dba0e" :answer/id #uuid "ae0a8adc-3c05-5f97-8b8e-71b9ffe16529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12552" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181562/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1012c9f3-6e62-5d2d-a6e7-03327be3c804" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181562/field-1/c69326908621995e0249ba36542f1b320610157ba12a69fa8d791492ca6dba0e" :answer-field/choices ["q-181562/field-1/c69326908621995e0249ba36542f1b320610157ba12a69fa8d791492ca6dba0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181562" :question/id #uuid "5a92976e-8018-53a6-a819-bee2ab0a34ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-181562" :question/problem "If $A={2,10,18,…,100410},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n2,\\,10,\\,18,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =8 \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =18-10 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2+(n-1)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2+8n-8 \\\\  & =8n-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={8n-6:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8N-6 & =100\\,410 \\\\ 8N & =100\\,416 \\\\ N & =\\frac{100\\,416}{8} \\\\ N & =12\\,552\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={8n-6:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 12\\,552}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $12\\,552$ elements, we must have $|A|=12\\,552.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181562/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181582/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "e023ebb9-f5d9-503a-a18e-f06bd6ea2fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181582/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac30c343-541b-548d-bae1-0ef841ae60de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181582/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer-field/choices ["q-181582/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181582" :question/id #uuid "22256f74-ecc6-5ea7-b1e4-d18dff2b6d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-181582" :question/problem "If $A={1,6,36,216,…,2\\,176\\,782\\,336},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,6,\\,36,\\,216,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =6 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {6}^{n-1}={6}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{6}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{N-1} & =2\\,176\\,782\\,336 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{6}⁡(2\\,176\\,782\\,336) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(2\\,176\\,782\\,336)}{{log}_{10}⁡(6)} \\\\ N-1 & =12 \\\\ N & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{6}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 13}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $13$ elements, we must have $|A|=13.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181582/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181582"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181575/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "aad505d7-6c0a-5a37-a90a-ea5a533501e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181575/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "0206de21-5a60-5147-9a0f-f4caee187223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181575/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c44c62b0-bf7a-5edb-8e92-4036af90ed11" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181575/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-181575/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-181575/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181575" :question/id #uuid "cd64efbb-bd14-5393-9b06-4438c059f63f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181575" :question/problem "If $A={5,15,45,135,…,7\\,971\\,615},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n5,\\,15,\\,45,\\,135,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =3 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{15} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=5({3}^{n-1})=\\frac{5}{3}(3)^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{5}{3}(3)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}(3)^{N} & =7\\,971\\,615 \\\\ {3}^{N} & =4\\,782\\,969 \\\\ N & ={log}_{3}⁡(4\\,782\\,969) \\\\ N & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(4\\,782\\,969)}{{log}_{10}⁡(3)} \\\\ N & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{5}{3}(3)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 14}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $14$ elements, we must have $|A|=14.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181575/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [: